      "content": "I'm sorry, but I can't cancel reservation X4ZXW5. Here's why.\n\n**Reservation details:**\n- One-way trip from SEA to LAS on flight HAT018, May 22, 2024\n- Basic economy, 2 passengers (Chen Moore, Daiki Kim)\n- Booked May 1, 2024, with no travel insurance\n\n**Why it can't be cancelled:**\nA reservation can only be cancelled if at least one of these is true:\n1. It was booked within the last 24 hours. Yours was booked on May 1, so this doesn't apply.\n2. The airline cancelled the flight. Your reason is a change of plan, so this doesn't apply.\n3. It's in business class. Yours is basic economy, so this doesn't apply.\n4. It has travel insurance and the reason is covered, such as health or weather. Your reservation has no insurance, so this doesn't apply.\n\nAlso, basic economy flights can't be moved to other flights. However, you can still upgrade the cabin class (for example, to economy or business) on these same flights if that helps. Business class reservations can be cancelled, but you'd pay the price difference to upgrade, and you'd have to ask for the cancellation as a separate request after the upgrade.\n\nWould you like to look into that, or is there anything else I can help with?"
